<h1 class="mb-6 text-3xl font-semibold text-gray-900">New exercise</h1>

<%# The movements this name might already be. #478.

    Folding (#474) settles whether two names *are* the same name, and it cannot settle this:
    "Squat" is not "Back Squat" by any spelling rule, and fifteen movements on the reporting
    account have "squat" in the name. A sixteenth was one submit away, with nothing said, and
    that is exactly how the legacy bare "Squat" in #445 came to exist.

    Asked rather than refused, because there is a person at this end who can answer. Each
    candidate is a link to the movement itself, so "did you mean this one" can be checked
    rather than guessed at -- the page it goes to shows the training already on it, which is
    the thing that actually answers the question.

    The confirm button carries new_exercise and posts the same fields back, so nothing typed
    is lost by being asked. The form below is re-rendered with its values intact for the same
    reason: a question that costs you your note is a question you learn to avoid. %>
<%- if @similar&.any? %>
  <div class="mb-6 rounded-lg border border-sky-800 bg-sky-50 px-4 py-3">
    <p class="text-sm text-gray-700">
      <%- if @similar.length == 1 %>
        You already have a movement this could be. Open it to check, or say yours is a
        different one.
      <%- else %>
        You already have <%= @similar.length %> movements this could be. Open one to check, or
        say yours is a different one.
      <%- end %>
    </p>
    <ul class="mt-2 space-y-1">
      <%- @similar.each do |movement| %>
        <li>
          <a href="/exercises/<%= movement.id %>/"
             class="text-sm font-semibold text-sky-800 underline hover:text-sky-900">
            <%= movement.name %>
          </a>
          <%- if movement.library? %>
            <span class="text-xs text-gray-500">from the shared library</span>
          <%- end %>
        </li>
      <%- end %>
    </ul>
    <%# A form of its own rather than a button inside the one below, because the fields it
        needs are the ones already typed and re-posting them is the whole point. Hidden inputs
        rather than a submit button added to the main form, so the ordinary Save keeps meaning
        "ask me again if it is still ambiguous" and only this one waves the question through. %>
    <form method="post" action="/exercises" class="mt-3">
      <%== csrf_tag('/exercises') %>
      <input type="hidden" name="name" value="<%= @exercise&.name %>">
      <input type="hidden" name="note" value="<%= @exercise&.note %>">
      <input type="hidden" name="dumbbell_count" value="<%= @exercise&.dumbbell_count %>">
      <%# The rest travels too, which it did not before 039 -- it was read off @exercise and
          the unsaved row here never carried it, so confirming a near-duplicate silently
          dropped the one field on this form that makes a noise. @rest is what the route kept
          from the post that raised the question. %>
      <input type="hidden" name="default_rest_seconds" value="<%= @rest %>">
      <%- if @exercise&.is_barbell %>
        <input type="hidden" name="is_barbell" value="1">
      <%- end %>
      <%- if @exercise&.default_is_per_side %>
        <input type="hidden" name="default_is_per_side" value="1">
      <%- end %>
      <input type="hidden" name="id" value="">
      <input type="hidden" name="new_exercise" value="1">
      <button type="submit"
              class="<%= button_style %> min-h-11 border border-sky-800 bg-sky-800 px-4 py-2 text-sm font-semibold text-white hover:bg-sky-900">
        No, <%= @exercise&.name %> is a different movement
      </button>
    </form>
  </div>
<%- end %>

<%== render('exercises/_form') %>
